message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Interface Closure and Representational Sealing: Three-Detector Simulation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kahl"
    given-names: "Peter"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1616-4843"

version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-28"

abstract: >-
  Computational supplement to 'What Conceptual Change Cannot Recover:
  Interface Closure and Representational Sealing'. The software implements
  a three-detector latent-class toy model illustrating the distinction
  between role-level identification, statistical label symmetry, and
  epistemic access to stipulated role-exceeding structure under interface
  closure.

keywords:
  - "representational sealing"
  - "interface closure"
  - "identifiability"
  - "latent-class models"
  - "conceptual change"
  - "epistemology"
  - "philosophy of science"

